From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@example.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 10:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] binutils: readelf: avoid off64_t on musl host builds

binutils 2.42 uses off64_t/fseeko64 when HAVE_FSEEKO64 is detected.
On musl host builds the function probe may succeed while the declarations
are not exposed to readelf.c, causing host tool compilation to fail with:

  error: unknown type name 'off64_t'
  warning: implicit declaration of function 'fseeko64'

For this build system we only need a portable host-side implementation.
Prefer fseeko/off_t when available and fall back to fseek/long.

--- a/binutils/readelf.c
+++ b/binutils/readelf.c
@@ -372,16 +372,10 @@ enum versioned_symbol_info
 static int
 fseek64 (FILE *stream, int64_t offset, int whence)
 {
-#if defined (HAVE_FSEEKO64)
-  off64_t o = offset;
-  if (o != offset)
-    {
-      errno = EINVAL;
-      return -1;
-    }
-  return fseeko64 (stream, o, whence);
-#elif defined (HAVE_FSEEKO)
+#if defined (HAVE_FSEEKO)
   off_t o = offset;
   if (o != offset)
     {
       errno = EINVAL;
       return -1;
